1
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:51,000
The truth is, we cannot speak other than by our paintings.

2
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:36,000
Loving Vincent is a animation, drama, mystery film directed by Hugh Welchman.

3
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:21,000
A young man arrives at the last hometown of painter Vincent van Gogh to deliver the
troubled artist's final letter and ends up investigating his final days there.

4
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:06,000
Armand Roulin, played by Douglas Booth.

5
00:23:45,000 --> 00:23:51,000
Vincent van Gogh, played by Robert Gulaczyk.

6
00:28:30,000 --> 00:28:36,000
Adeline Ravoux, played by Eleanor Tomlinson.

7
00:33:15,000 --> 00:33:21,000
Louise Chevalier, played by Helen McCrory.

8
00:38:00,000 --> 00:38:06,000
Marguerite Gachet, played by Saoirse Ronan.

9
00:42:45,000 --> 00:42:51,000
Postman Joseph Roulin, played by Chris O'Dowd.

10
00:47:30,000 --> 00:47:36,000
Loving Vincent is a 2017 experimental animated historical drama film about the life of the
painter Vincent van Gogh, in particular the circumstances of his death.

11
00:52:15,000 --> 00:52:21,000
It is the first fully painted animated feature film.

12
00:57:00,000 --> 00:57:06,000
The film, written and directed  by Dorota Kobiela and Hugh Welchman, is a Polish-UK co-production,
funded by the Polish Film Institute, and partially through a Kickstarter campaign.

13
01:01:45,000 --> 01:01:51,000
First conceived as a seven-minute short film in 2008, Loving Vincent was realized by Dorota Kobiela, a
painter herself, after studying the techniques and the artist's story through his letters.

14
01:06:30,000 --> 01:06:36,000
With an additional use of rotoscoping animation, each of the film's 65,000 frames is an oil painting on canvas,
created using the same techniques as Van Gogh by a team of 125 artists drawn from around the globe.

15
01:11:15,000 --> 01:11:21,000
The film premiered at the 2017 Annecy International Animated Film Festival.

16
01:16:00,000 --> 01:16:06,000
The film received critical acclaim and won Best Animated Feature Film Award at the 30th European Film
Awards in Berlin and was nominated for Best Animated Feature at the 90th Academy Awards.

17
01:20:45,000 --> 01:20:51,000
The film marked Helen McCrory's final film role before her death in April 2021.

18
01:25:30,000 --> 01:25:36,000
The film explores themes of artist, investigation, grave, letter, melancholy.

19
01:30:15,000 --> 01:30:21,000
The tone is emotional and mind_bending.
